WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.000
[On-screen text] Room to Read presents

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.500
[On-screen text] In association with the Troper Wojcicki Foundation

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.000
[On-screen text] Executive Producers: Brenda Chapman, Jill Culton, Freida Pinto, Dr. Geetha Murali, Nexus Studios

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.000
[On-screen text] SHE Creates Change

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Right now, 122 million girls around the world are not in school. Millions more risk falling behind or dropping out.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:40.000
This is the true story of six courageous girls who overcame gender discrimination and fought to stay in school.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:53.500
[On-screen text] Dewmini — Sri Lanka

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:04.000
We used to live in a small house back then.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.500
We didn't have much to eat and drink.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.000
We had economic difficulties.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.500
Some days I fainted in school,

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.000
because I didn't have breakfast.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:29.000
They tried to send me to a house in the city to work.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.000
Nobody asked me if I wanted to go.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.000
It was the most difficult moment of my life.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:41.000
[On-screen text] Dewmini lifted her family out of poverty by learning to garden in drought conditions. She stayed in school and plans to help local farmers adapt to climate change.
